abstract: >
  perceptome is an open-source Python toolkit implementing a 44-module cellular
  perception framework with four analytic layers: geometry (44 regulatory modules
  placed in a fixed 9-dimensional eigenspace derived from 154 Human Protein Atlas
  normal cell types, in the standardized coordinates of Spiro 2026), convergence
  (the assay of that paper: assignment of single cells to the nearest of 152 normal
  cell types, occupancy of the convergence region, and the within-patient test of
  whether malignant epithelium occupies that region more often than the same
  patient's normal epithelium), perceptivity (5-vector capacity / engagement /
  specialization metric per cell type, with the upward-asymmetric capacity-floor
  predictor closed across substrate-series Papers 4.5 - 4.8), and validity
  (random-200 / housekeeping / cell-cycle scorecard for perturbation analyses).
  Includes the Paper 4.2 cancer capacity-direction reference (P3 PASS, Sun 2021
  paired HCC) and a focused 9-anchor drug operation matching the narrow validated
  scope from Paper 4.1 (6 mechanism-pathway rescues + 3 stress-axis controls; 11
  falsified drug operations explicitly NOT supported). NPAS4 is the 44th canonical
  module per Paper 4.
